cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or this code, please cite the paper and this repository."
title: "Benchmark accuracy does not predict field accuracy: an error budget for automated species identification in environmental monitoring"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data for a measurement of what a benchmark accuracy is worth
  once the conditions of deployment stop matching the conditions of the
  benchmark: 5,969 images of 152 fern species in 30 families from iNaturalist and
  GBIF, per-image annotations of image domain, data source and country, grouped
  splits by observation, 700 open-set negatives in eight groups, 262 annotated
  label boxes for a masked-label control, and 32 released experimental runs.
type: software
license:
